{"toolCallId":"call_69a86b7e5713467796f7d7d0fd0e0e45","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/memory-system.md:85:  --json -- \"<prompt>\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/memory-system.md:94:One output mode per invocation. Combining `--json` with `--count` or `--files-with-matches` is not rejected; the last flag wins silently, and a JSONL parser handed count output sees an empty result rather than an error.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/memory-system.md:139:rg --no-config --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case -C 2 \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/memory-system.md:230:  --json -- \"spec folder\"; echo \"exit=$?\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/memory-system.md:233:rg --no-config --fixed-strings --ignore-case --files-with-matches --max-count 1 \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/save-workflow.md:217:  --json '{\"specFolder\":\"049-anchor-context-retrieval\",\"sessionSummary\":\"Implemented anchor retrieval...\"}' \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/save-workflow.md:404:Spec documents are retrieved from the working tree, never from a database. The committed trigger index answers Gate 1 through `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"<prompt>\"`, and free-text retrieval follows the ripgrep recipes in `references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md`, scoped by track and packet. Retrieval is lexical only: paraphrase, fusion, decay and access tracking are unsupported, and a miss is a clean no-hit.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/trigger-config.md:94:  --json -- \"I want to save context for this session\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/memory/trigger-config.md:132:  --json -- \"refactor the authentication module\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/config/environment-variables.md:110:node runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json '{\"specFolder\":\"001-feature\",\"sessionSummary\":\"...\"}' specs/001-feature/\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:80:  --files-with-matches --max-count 1 --glob '*.md' \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:87:rg --json --count -- 'phrase' specs\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:93:rg --no-config --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:164:node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"spec folder\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:170:rg --no-config --fixed-strings --ignore-case --files-with-matches --max-count 1 \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:195:node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"recent work\"; echo \"exit=$?\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:218:node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"test\"; echo \"exit=$?\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:221:rg --no-config --fixed-strings --ignore-case --files-with-matches \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:274:rg --no-config --fixed-strings --ignore-case --files-with-matches --max-count 1 \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:295:rg --no-config --fixed-strings --ignore-case --files-with-matches \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/debugging/troubleshooting.md:403:node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"<prompt>\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md:41:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh --json specs/001-feature/\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md:58:Verifies the verification checklist in `tasks.md` and, when `acceptance-criteria.md` exists, that every criterion is Met or waived against a decision record, before claiming \"done\". The sentinel Stop hook reads its `--json` output on every completion claim.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md:66:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-completion.sh --json specs/001-feature/\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md:89:node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json '{\"specFolder\":\"001-feature\",\"sessionSummary\":\"...\"}' specs/001-feature/\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/cli/memory-handback.md:32:5. **Choose a structured-input mode**: Save the scrubbed payload to `/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json`, pipe it with `--stdin`, or pass it inline with `--json`.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/cli/memory-handback.md:36:   - `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json \"$JSON_PAYLOAD\" [spec-folder]`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/cli/memory-handback.md:45:**Structured JSON only**: Direct spec-folder-only invocation is no longer supported. Always call `generate-context.js` with `--stdin`, `--json`, or a JSON temp file.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/cli/daemon-cli-reference.md:57:node .skilled/bin/<cli>.cjs <tool_name> [--json '{...}'] [--format json|text|jsonl] [--timeout-ms N] [--warm-only]\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/cli/daemon-cli-reference.md:70:Use `--json` for one complete JSON object argument when a tool has structured input:\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/cli/daemon-cli-reference.md:73:node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"implement cli core\"}' --format json --timeout-ms 3000 --warm-only\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/cli/daemon-cli-reference.md:88:`jsonl` is not streaming JSON Lines. Do not assume one record per tool, one record per result, or incremental output. When passing input with `--json`, pass one complete JSON object as one shell argument; the CLI does not parse a stream of JSONL records from stdin.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/cli/daemon-cli-reference.md:98:| `64` | Usage or schema error | Bad flags, invalid `--json`, schema validation failure, or advisor trusted-mutation refusal. |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md:85:rg --no-config --hidden --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md:96:  --files-with-matches --max-count 1 \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md:116:rg --no-config --hidden --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case -C 2 \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md:133:`--json` cannot be combined with the path-only mode (`-l` or `--files-with-matches`), the count mode (`-c` or `--count`) or `--count-matches`. Each output mode is its own recipe, and the wrapper parses one shape at a time.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md:135:> **Observed hazard, re-tested at ripgrep 15.2.0.** Combining them is not rejected. The last output-mode flag on the command line wins silently. `rg --json --count` returned count lines and `rg --count --json` returned JSONL, both at exit `0`. A wrapper that sets both flags therefore gets whichever it happened to write last, and a JSONL parser handed count output sees an empty result rather than an error. Do not rely on ripgrep to catch this.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md:154:  --files-with-matches --max-count 1 --glob '*.md' \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/level-specifications.md:765:- Use `/speckit:save` or `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json '{\"specFolder\":\"...\",\"sessionSummary\":\"...\"}' specs/###-folder/`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-guide.md:623:**Creation (JSON mode — preferred):** `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json '{\"specFolder\":\"###-name\",\"sessionSummary\":\"...\"}' specs/###-name/`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/grep-convention.md:266:rg --no-config --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/grep-convention.md:275:  --files-with-matches --max-count 1 \\\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/grep-convention.md:300:- `--json` cannot be combined with `--files`, `--files-with-matches`, `--count` or `--count-matches`. Parse match records in the wrapper instead of mixing output modes.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:804:| `SPECKIT_SKIP_VALIDATION` | unset | Set to `1`, `true`, `yes` or `on` to skip validation, in the environment or saved in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env`. The environment wins over the file. A skipped run exits 0 and under `--json` prints a report marked `skipped: true` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/path-scoped-rules.md:112:.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/007-feature/ --json\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/path-scoped-rules.md:126:| `SPECKIT_SKIP_VALIDATION` | unset   | Set to `1`, `true`, `yes` or `on` to skip every rule and exit 0. Also read from `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env`, and a set environment value wins over the file even when it is `0` or empty. Under `--json` a skipped run still prints a report, marked `skipped: true` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/phase-checklists.md:128:- [ ] Save context if significant progress: `/speckit:save` or `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json '{\"specFolder\":\"...\",\"sessionSummary\":\"...\"}' specs/###-folder/`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/phase-checklists.md:159:- [ ] Memory context saved: `/speckit:save` or `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json '{\"specFolder\":\"...\",\"sessionSummary\":\"...\"}' specs/###-folder/`\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"95fbd7","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
