{"toolCallId":"call_83e5bcae39bf427f827da9f3675a44fe","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"== pipes in backticks on table lines ==\nspec.md:75:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add `--quiet`/`-q` parsing, one shared level-line function and the help entry |\nspec.md:177:| R-003 | `-q` collides with a future flag | L | L | `-q` already means quiet in `validate.sh` and `check-completion.sh`, so the short form is the repo convention |\nplan.md:89:| `recommend-level.sh` case loop (`:656-719`) | Owns flag parsing | Update | `grep -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` shows one case arm. `--quiet` is accepted, unknown options still exit 1. |\nplan.md:90:| `output_text()` (`:508-558`) | Sole producer of the `Recommended Level:` literal | Update | `grep -rn 'Recommended Level:' runtime` returns one hit, inside the shared helper |\nplan.md:91:| `output_json()` (`:560-649`) | Machine-readable output | Unchanged | `diff <(--json) <(--json --quiet)` is empty |\nplan.md:92:| `show_help()` (`:162-211`) and the header comment block | Option documentation | Update | `--help` lists `--quiet, -q` |\nplan.md:93:| `runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js` | Programmatic consumer, JSON only | Unchanged | Suite reports `passed=27 failed=0` |\nplan.md:94:| `runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js` | Programmatic consumer, JSON only | Unchanged | Suite reports `passed=51 failed=0` |\nplan.md:95:| Seven files under `references/` | Mention the script by purpose and example | Unchanged | No file lists `--loc`, `--files` or `--json` as recommend-level options, so there is no option list to sync |\nacceptance-criteria.md:56:| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given valid numeric inputs, When `--quiet` is passed, Then stdout is exactly `Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)` | `recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet` prints that line and nothing else | Unmet | - |\nacceptance-criteria.md:57:| AC-002 | REQ-001 | Given the same inputs, When `-q` is passed instead, Then stdout matches AC-001 byte for byte | `diff` between the `-q` run and the `--quiet` run is empty | Unmet | - |\nacceptance-criteria.md:58:| AC-003 | REQ-002 | Given any accepted input, When `--quiet` is passed, Then stdout is one line whose first byte is `R`, not a newline | `... --quiet | wc -l` reports 1, and `... --quiet | od -c` shows `R` first | Unmet | - |\nacceptance-criteria.md:60:| AC-005 | REQ-003 | Given any accepted input, When `--quiet` is absent, Then stdout is byte-identical to the captured baseline | `diff` against `scratch/baseline/` across all 20 matrix rows | Unmet | - |\nacceptance-criteria.md:62:| AC-007 | REQ-004 | Given no `--loc` and no `--files`, When `--quiet` is passed, Then stderr carries the error, stdout is empty and the exit code is 1 | `... --quiet >out 2>err; echo $?` reports 1, `wc -c out` reports 0, `err` contains `ERROR: At least --loc or --files must be provided` | Unmet | - |\nacceptance-criteria.md:64:| AC-009 | REQ-005 | Given `--help`, When it runs, Then the output lists `--quiet, -q` with a description | `recommend-level.sh --help | grep -- '--quiet, -q'` finds the entry | Unmet | - |\nacceptance-criteria.md:65:| AC-010 | REQ-006 | Given `--json`, When `--quiet` is added, Then the JSON document is unchanged | `diff <(... --json) <(... --json --quiet)` is empty for the documented fixtures | Unmet | - |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"418436","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
