ither output\" was wrong for the flags | Drop both. The flags drop on low stakes and missing gold for which level a packet should have had, not on a missing reader |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:1066:| 22 | Spec-level risk flags beside the level script | The level script reads the flags (auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20), so a Jev flag would change a level. It drops on low stakes and on missing gold for which level a packet should have had, not on a missing reader | Q3, Q11 | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` | DeepSeek parked it as later. Dropped here |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:1473:| 180 | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` | Council | resolved | Risk flags add points to the level. Row 22 and disagreement 7 corrected (K12) |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:1596:- `runtime/cli/spec-folder/alignment-validator.ts` and `runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mimo/iterations/iteration-006.md:106:| **Value** | Both add a signal to surfaces the operator already resolves fine: `recommend-level.sh` takes four explicit flags whose answers the caller knows, and S25's HIGH issues are already patched by hand. Neither removes a decision; both add a number to check. |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mimo/iterations/iteration-006.md:107:| **Seam** | S24 `recommend-level.sh:19-22` and S25 `save-workflow.md:577-598` (seam-map claims). |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/research.md:80:9. **Spec-level risk flags — LATER.** `recommend-level.sh` (digest S24); weak gold; policy semantics owned by the script.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md:56:| **Idea** | `noul` per risk flag (\"does this task change authentication / APIs / data / architecture\") so `recommend-level.sh` stops depending on the caller's memory. |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md:57:| **Seam** | S24 `recommend-level.sh:19-22`, `:42-47`, `:106-109` (digest); offline CLI, points map to Levels 0-3. |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/seats/round-001/seat-001-opus-max.md:123:- **(c) Defer log and spec-level flags.** Both drops hold. The level-flag reason, \"no decision reads either output\" (`research.md:351`), is wrong: each flag adds points that set the level (`recommend-level.sh:19-22`, `:36-47`). The correct reason is low stakes (one documentation tier), no gold and the same task text an agent already reads.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/seats/round-001/seat-001-opus-max.md:135:| 22 | drop | keep, fix reason | drop | The flags feed the level, so \"no decision reads it\" is wrong. Drop on low stakes and no gold | `recommend-level.sh:19-22`, `:36-47` | Confirmed |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/seats/round-001/seat-001-opus-max.md:352:  - `recommend-level.sh:15-50`, `:100-112`\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/proposed-resynthesis.md:245:- The level script does read the spec-level flags (`recommend-level.sh:36-47`: auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20), so \"no decision reads either output\" was wrong for the flags.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/proposed-resynthesis.md:473:  - The level script reads the flags (`recommend-level.sh:36-47`: auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20), so a Jev flag would change a level.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/propose