.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/evidence-marker-audit.ts,.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/generated-metadata-drift.ts,.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/generated-metadata-integrity.ts,.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/unactioned-recorded-failure-audit.mjs,.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/scripts/run-tests-sharded.mjs,.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/scripts/run-tests.mjs,.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/scripts/env-reader-table.mjs (this iteration's slice). The full 273-file scope is reviewScopeFiles in specs/sk-code/011-sk-code-poinytail-based-refinement/020-open-ends-research/005-silent-input-sweep/review/deep-review-config.json\n./specs/sk-code/011-sk-code-poinytail-based-refinement/020-open-ends-research/005-silent-input-sweep/review/iterations/iteration-010.md:15:- .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:713 — `*` reject, exit 1; all documented options handled (:690, :694, :698, :706, :710)\n./specs/sk-code/011-sk-code-poinytail-based-refinement/020-open-ends-research/005-silent-input-sweep/review/iterations/iteration-010.md:154:CONDITIONAL — 1 P1 (no P0) this iteration. Sixteen of the 29 files are strict parsers that reject unknown options with a non-zero exit (quality-audit, recommend-level, refresh-track-roots, repair-derived, sweep-track-roots, sync-phase-map-status, template-phrase-census, template-phrase-cleanup, upgrade-legacy, upgrade-level, validate.sh, continuity-freshness, generated-metadata-drift, generated-metadata-integrity, scaffold-debug-delegation, template-structure); the remaining defects cluster in audit/report helpers that silently absorb stray or mis-consumed tokens, plus one documented check-mode CLI (`env-reader-table --check`) that a typo converts into an exit-0 no-op.\n./specs/sk-code/011-sk-code-poinytail-based-refinement/028-surface-setup-hardening-research/goal.md:77:| Packet scaffolded | Done | create.sh phase mode with `--with-goal` under the 011 epic at Level 1; recommend-level.sh printed Level 0 (Quick) for `--loc 0 --files 3`, and Level 1 is the lowest create.sh writes |\n./specs/sk-code/011-sk-code-poinytail-based-refinement/009-round-two-follow-ups/004-agents-md-pointers/scratch/dryrun/AGENTS.md:251:| **Which level does this work need?**                                | `system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` — deterministic scoring over LOC, file count and risk. |\n./specs/sk-code/011-sk-code-poinytail-based-refinement/009-round-two-follow-ups/004-agents-md-pointers/scratch/before/AGENTS.md:251:| **Which level does this work need?**                                | `system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` — deterministic scoring over LOC, file count and risk. |\n./specs/sk-design/018-sk-design-parent-v2/001-sk-create-chart/010-chart-review-remediation/spec.md:204:Scored with `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc 1100 --files 34 --api --architectural`, which returned **Level 3 (Full) at 83 of 100**, confidence 94%. The API flag is passed because the check's rule surface gains a name that other documents index. The architectural flag is passed because the table pan region is a markup convention added to every file in the corpus rather than a change inside one.\n./specs/sk-design/018-sk-design-parent-v2/001-sk-create-chart/009-chart-visual-overhaul/002-chrome-rollout/spec.md:271:`recommend-level.sh --loc 1050 --files 33 --architectural --api` returns Level 3 at 83 of 100,\n./specs/sk-design/018-sk-design-parent-v2/001-sk-create-chart/009-chart-visual-overhaul/001-visual-proof-and-forks/spec.md:223:`recommend-level.sh --loc 300 --files 12 --architectural` returns Level 2 at 57 of 100, with a\n./specs/sk-design/018-sk-design-parent-v2/001-sk-create-chart/009-chart-visual-overhaul/004-interaction-layer/goal.md:101:| Recommended level | Done | `recommend-level.sh --loc 800 --files 15 --architect