 dump)]\n./specs/system-speckit/033-system-speckit-v4/030-spec-kit-simplification-research/011-command-surface-contract-realignment/implementation-summary.md:57:Every level's required files now match the manifest. The completion workflow's fifth step authors `acceptance-criteria.md`, one row per requirement, and its eleventh step sets every row to Met, Waived or Superseded and checks the P0 and P1 items of the tasks.md verification checklist; the implementation workflow's fourth step does the same; the resume workflow reads the closure document instead of the retired one. The inline scaffold, the evidence sources, the enforcement notes and the presentation lines follow. Every `level_contract_*` name became the template's real path, and the level-selection note names `recommend-level.sh`. Eighteen comment lines lost their ticket ids and kept their reasons.\n./specs/system-speckit/033-system-speckit-v4/030-spec-kit-simplification-research/011-command-surface-contract-realignment/spec.md:49:- Command workflows that scaffold, verify and report the acceptance-criteria document and the tasks.md verification checklist instead of the retired `checklist.md`, name real template paths, and defer level choice to `recommend-level.sh`\n./specs/system-speckit/033-system-speckit-v4/066-pre-v4-spec-upgrade/spec.md:210:| Scope | 15/25 | About 12 files, about 900 LOC per `recommend-level.sh` |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/015-anchor-enforcement-automation/scratch/wave1-context-investigations.md:21:- validate.sh, check-placeholders.sh, recommend-level.sh\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/tasks.md:89:- [x] T001 [P0] Add `determine_phasing()` function to `recommend-level.sh` with 5 phase signal scoring dimensions (`.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/tasks.md:90:- [x] T002 [P0] Add `--recommend-phases` CLI flag to include phase scoring in output [B: T001] (`.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/tasks.md:91:- [x] T003 [P1] Add `--phase-threshold <N>` CLI flag for threshold override (default 25) [B: T001] (`.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/tasks.md:92:- [x] T004 [P0] Extend JSON output with `recommended_phases`, `phase_score`, `phase_reason`, `suggested_phase_count` [B: T001, T002] (`.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-3-scoring-correctness.md:3:**Reviewed file:** `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh`\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-3-scoring-correctness.md:35:### Script values (recommend-level.sh, lines 85-89):\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-3-scoring-correctness.md:258:Reconcile the point values between `recommend-level.sh` and `phase_definitions.md`. Either:\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:17:| Dimension | `recommend-level.sh` (lines 85-89) | `phase_definitions.md` (lines 39-46) | `spec.md` REQ-001 (line 140) |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:29:   - Script source: `recommend-level.sh` line 85: `readonly PHASE_POINTS_ARCHITECTURAL=15`\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:34:   - Script source: `recommend-level.sh` line 89: `readonly PHASE_POINTS_EXTREME_SCALE=5`\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:39:   - Script source: `recommend-level.sh` lines 415-416: `if [[ \"$FILES\" -gt 30 ]] || [[ \"$LOC\" -gt 2000 ]]` — Triggers when files > 30 OR LOC > 2000\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:56:| `recommend-level.sh` | **25** | Line 91: `readonly PHASE_DEFAULT_THRESHOLD=25` |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:73:| Score Range | `recommend-level.sh` (lines 436-443) | `phase_definitions.md` (lines 62-66) |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:110:| Step 1 (Analyze Scope) | `recommend-level.sh --json --recommend-phases --phase-threshold {phase_threshold} --loc ... --files ...` | Lines 143-144 | Lines 160-161 | YES |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:117:**Note:** The script paths are relative in the YAML (e.g., `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh`), which is correct for project-root execution context.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:161:- Phase detection/scoring via `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases`\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:177:- **Search for exact terms:** `phase system|phase decomposition|phase folder|phase workflow|recommend-level.*phase` returned zero matches.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:183:- Phase detection via `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases`\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-10-cross-consistency.md:224:| recommend-level.sh | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh` | 776 |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-1-recommend-level-standards.md:1:# Agent 1: Shell Standards Verification — recommend-level.sh\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/scratch/agent-1-recommend-level-standards.md:3:**File under review:** `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh` (776 lines)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:45:This plan covers formalizing the organic phase decomposition pattern that emerged from specs 136 and 138 into a first-class SpecKit behavioral layer. The technical approach adds phase detection to `recommend-level.sh`, structured creation to `create.sh`, a new `/spec_kit:phase` command, and recursive validation to `validate.sh` — all as additive changes that leave existing flat specs unaffected.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:51:2. **Script System** (`.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/`): 9 lifecycle scripts. `create.sh` has `--subfolder` mode that auto-increments `[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/` numbering, copies level templates, creates `scratch/`. No git branch for sub-folders. `recommend-level.sh` scores on 4 dimensions (LOC 35%, files 20%, risk 25%, complexity 20%) with thresholds 0-24=skip, 25-44=L1, 45-69=L2, 70+=L3. No phase scoring exists.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:90:- [ ] Phase detection: recommend-level.sh with --recommend-phases, 5 fixtures passing\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:130:- **recommend-level.sh**: Extended with phase scoring dimension and --recommend-phases flag\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:141:         recommend-level.sh (enhanced with --recommend-phases)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:170:### Phase 1: Detection & Scoring (recommend-level.sh enhancement)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:174:**Changes to `recommend-level.sh`:**\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:292:1. Analyze request scope → run recommend-level.sh with phase scoring\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:366:| recommend-level.sh phase scoring | Shell test fixtures | 5 fixtures: below/at/above threshold, extreme, no-risk |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:398:| recommend-level.sh scoring framework | Internal | Phase 1 | Working (4-dimension scoring) | Blocks phase dimension addition |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:489:│  (recommend-level.sh)    │──────┐                       │\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:511:| recommend-level.sh (phase scoring) | None | Phase score JSON, --recommend-phases output | create.sh --phase design, SKILL.md PHASE intent |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:544:| M1: Phase Detection Ready | recommend-level.sh with --recommend-phases, 5 test fixtures passing | Run scoring against 136/138 profiles — both should trigger phases=true | End of Phase 1 |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:562:**Files**: recommend-level.sh (scoring logic), 5 new test fixtures\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:630:| W-A | Detection & Scoring | @general | .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh, test fixtures (5) | Mostly Complete (T005 fixture pending) |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/plan.md:661:| G2: Phase 1 Complete | recommend-level.sh tests pass | Updated script, 5 test fixtures | Self-review |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/spec.md:53:**Key Decisions**: (1) Phases are a behavioral layer on top of existing levels, not a new level tier; (2) Auto-suggestion via enhanced `recommend-level.sh` scoring; (3) New `/spec_kit:phase` command for phase lifecycle management.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/spec.md:93:- Phase detection scoring in `recommend-level.sh` (new `--recommend-phases` output)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/spec.md:119:| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add phase recommendation scoring and --recommend-phases flag |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/spec.md:149:| REQ-001 | `recommend-level.sh` outputs phase recommendation alongside level recommendation | `--json` output includes `recommended_phases: true/false`, `phase_reason`, `suggested_phase_count` when level score >= 70 (100-point scale) AND (architectural OR files > 15 OR LOC > 800) |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/spec.md:161:| REQ-008 | Auto-suggestion triggers when AI detects task exceeding phase thresholds | AI proactively suggests \"This task may benefit from a phased approach\" when recommend-level.sh scoring indicates phases |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/spec.md:172:| REQ-014 | `recommend-level.sh` suggests phase names based on task decomposition | JSON output includes `suggested_phase_names[]` when phases recommended |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/spec.md:181:- **SC-001**: Phase recommendation accuracy - `recommend-level.sh` correctly identifies tasks needing phases (validated against 136/138 retrospective); target >= 80%\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/spec.md:191:- **When** `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json` evaluates the request\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/spec.md:250:- **NFR-P01**: `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases` adds < 50ms to scoring time\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/spec.md:326:**Acceptance**: When `recommend-level.sh --json --loc 2000 --files 25 --architectural --api --db` runs, output includes `\"recommended_phases\": true, \"suggested_phase_count\": 3`.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/decision-record.md:93:- Phase detection is a separate output from recommend-level.sh (two distinct outputs instead of one). Mitigation: Document the dual-output in the script's --help and in CLAUDE.md\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/decision-record.md:126:- `recommend-level.sh` — adds second output: phase recommendation (boolean + score) alongside level recommendation\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/decision-record.md:129:**How to roll back**: Remove the `--phase` flag handling from create.sh and the phase score output from recommend-level.sh. Existing phase folders remain valid as standard sub-folders; remove Phase Documentation Map sections from parent specs manually if desired.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/decision-record.md:252:recommend-level.sh needs a threshold to decide when to suggest phases. The threshold could be aggressive (suggest phases for any L2+ task) or conservative (only for demonstrably large, complex tasks). Over-suggestion degrades the UX for the common case — the majority of tasks are routine and phases add overhead without benefit. Under-suggestion means large tasks miss the guidance, but users can always invoke /spec_kit:phase manually.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/decision-record.md:268:**How it works**: recommend-level.sh computes a phase score (0-50) alongside the level recommendation. A phase suggestion fires only when both conditions are met: score >= 25 and recommended level is L3 or L3+. The threshold is configurable via --phase-threshold flag and a .speckit.yaml project override, so teams can adjust without modifying the script.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/decision-record.md:328:- `recommend-level.sh` — adds phase scoring algorithm (50-point scale), phase threshold check (>= 25 AND level >= 3), second output line for phase recommendation\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/decision-record.md:330:- `create.sh` — reads phase recommendation from recommend-level.sh when invoked without explicit flags\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/decision-record.md:332:**How to roll back**: Remove the phase scoring block and second output line from recommend-level.sh. Remove phase-threshold from .speckit.yaml schema. create.sh reverts to level-only recommendation input.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/021-spec-kit-phase-system/decision-record.md:470:**We chose**: Option E shown only when at least one of three conditions is met: (1) an existing spec folder is detected with high complexity markers, (2) the user's task description contains phase-related keywords, or (3) recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases returns true.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/018-rewrite-system-speckit-readme/scratch/research-brief.md:313:| `recommend-level.sh` | Recommend documentation level with phased decomposition detection |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/005-architecture-audit/scratch/z-archive-prior-audit/agent3-root-source-inventory.md:111:| .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh | Recommends level for the spec lifecycle automation workflow. | spec lifecycle automation | None detected |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/005-architecture-audit/scratch/z-archive-prior-audit/agent1-root-tree-readme-config.md:177:|   |   |-- recommend-level.sh\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/005-architecture-audit/scratch/z-archive-prior-audit/readme-audit-A20.md:12:`archive.sh`, `calculate-completeness.sh`, `check-completion.sh`, `check-placeholders.sh`, `create.sh`, `progressive-validate.sh`, `recommend-level.sh`, `test-validation.sh`, `upgrade-level.sh`, `validate.sh`\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/011-skill-alignment/scratch/agent-07-skill-integration.md:41:  - `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json specs/<spec>`\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/011-skill-alignment/scratch/agent-09-refs-workflows.md:52:- **Gap 7:** No execution method for `recommend-level.sh` (§6) with `--phase` flag or for Level 3+ scenarios. The existing flag table stops at `--architectural` (forces Level 3), with no flag for multi-phase/epic classification. (P2)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/011-skill-alignment/scratch/agent-09-refs-workflows.md:153:15. **Extend `recommend-level.sh` documentation** in `execution_methods.md` with a Level 3+ classification flag and multi-phase detection logic.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/009-perfect-session-capturing/016-json-mode-hybrid-enrichment/001-initial-enrichment/scratch/agent-output-iter-001-A3.md:26:Compare the spec-kit-phase-system memory (older, likely manually curated): `[\"spec kit phase system\", \"spec 139\", \"phase decomposition workflow\", \"spec kit:phase\", \"recommend-level phasing\"]` -- 5 precise, domain-relevant phrases. Versus the architecture-audit memory (auto-extracted): 30 phrases dominated by function names (`\"estimate token count\"`, `\"extract quality score\"`), path tokens (`\"kit/022\"`, `\"fusion/005\"`), and fragments (`\"and missing\"`, `\"audit\"`). The manually curated set would perform dramatically better in trigger matching because every phrase maps to a real retrieval intent.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/006-feature-catalog/research/deep-research-gap-report-2026-03-26.md:91:- **16 Tooling (4 gaps):** spec lifecycle scripts (create.sh, validate.sh, check-completion.sh, archive.sh, recommend-level.sh), template compose, memory tooling, core scripts\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/006-feature-catalog/scratch/verification-C18.md:528:.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp_server/INSTALL_GUIDE.md:472:The server supports phase folders for multi-phase spec work. Phase folders follow the pattern `specs/NNN-name/001-phase/`. Use the `--recursive` flag in `validate.sh` to validate all phases in a spec folder at once. The `recommend-level.sh` script applies phase detection scoring automatically.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/015-manual-testing-per-playbook/016-tooling-and-scripts/implementation-summary.md:51:| 1 | PHASE-001 | Phase detection scoring | PASS | recommend-level.sh:37-40,582-584 -- `recommended_phases`, `phase_score`, `suggested_phase_count`, 4 dimensions at 35%/20%/25%/20% |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/015-manual-testing-per-playbook/016-tooling-and-scripts/implementation-summary.md:167:- Shell scripts (recommend-level.sh, create.sh, validate.sh, check-phase-links.sh, progressive-validate.sh): grep and read for flag support, output fields, exit code handling\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/015-manual-testing-per-playbook/016-tooling-and-scripts/tasks.md:59:  - PHASE-001: Phase detection scoring -- **PASS** -- `recommend-level.sh` implements `--recommend-phases --json`, outputs `recommended_phases` (boolean), `phase_score` (number), `suggested_phase_count` (number), 4 dimensions at 35%/20%/25%/20% weights (scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh:37-40, 582-584)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/015-manual-testing-per-playbook/016-tooling-and-scripts/tasks.md:63:  - PHASE-005: Phase command workflow -- **PASS** -- `/spec_kit:phase` command exists with auto/confirm modes, 7-step workflow referencing recommend-level.sh, create.sh, check-phase-links.sh, validate.sh (command/spec_kit/phase.md)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/007-code-audit-per-feature-catalog/research/deep-research-gap-report-2026-03-26.md:91:- **16 Tooling (4 gaps):** spec lifecycle scripts (create.sh, validate.sh, check-completion.sh, archive.sh, recommend-level.sh), template compose, memory tooling, core scripts\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/069-speckit-template-complexity/plan.md:390:| recommend-level.sh | Extend | Green | Core algorithm to build upon |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/069-speckit-template-complexity/plan.md:412:- `recommend-level.sh`: 534 LOC, scoring algorithm foundation\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/069-speckit-template-complexity/spec.md:58:- The existing `recommend-level.sh` scoring algorithm provides a valid foundation to extend\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/069-speckit-template-complexity/spec.md:75:- Integration with existing `create-spec-folder.sh` and `recommend-level.sh`\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/069-speckit-template-complexity/spec.md:268:| recommend-level.sh | Internal | SpecKit | Green | Core extension point |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/069-speckit-template-complexity/spec.md:318:- **Existing Scripts**: recommend-level.sh (534 LOC), create-spec-folder.sh (822 LOC)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/069-speckit-template-complexity/decision-record.md:30:The existing `recommend-level.sh` uses 4 factors (LOC, files, risk, complexity) but doesn't capture research requirements or multi-agent coordination needs. Analysis of specs 056-068 shows significant variance in these dimensions.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/069-speckit-template-complexity/decision-record.md:182:## ADR-006: Extend recommend-level.sh vs Replace\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/069-speckit-template-complexity/decision-record.md:188:`recommend-level.sh` has a working scoring algorithm (534 LOC). Need to decide whether to extend or replace it.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/069-speckit-template-complexity/decision-record.md:192:- Keep `recommend-level.sh` for backward compatibility\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/087-speckit-deep-analysis/known-limitations.md:322:| `recommend-level.sh` | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/recommend-level.sh` | 534 | Automated level recommendation replacing manual LOC estimation. 4-dimension scoring: LOC (35%), files (20%), risk (25%), complexity (20%). Level mapping: <25=L0, 25-44=L1, 45-69=L2, 70+=L3. |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/087-speckit-deep-analysis/known-limitations.md:328:| `speckit.md` Capability Scan (lines 188-193) | `create.sh`, `validate.sh`, `calculate-completeness.sh` | `archive.sh`, `check-completion.sh`, `recommend-level.sh` |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/087-speckit-deep-analysis/known-limitations.md:329:| `SKILL.md` Key Scripts table (lines 192-199) | `generate-context.js`, `validate.sh`, `create.sh`, `compose.sh` | `archive.sh`, `check-completion.sh`, `recommend-level.sh` |\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/087-speckit-deep-analysis/known-limitations.md:333:- `recommend-level.sh` could replace the manual LOC/complexity estimation the speckit agent currently performs — a deterministic scoring script exists but agents don't know about it\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/087-speckit-deep-analysis/known-limitations.md:341:3. **Consider integrating** `recommend-level.sh` into the spec folder creation workflow (Option B in Gate 3)\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/074-speckit-template-optimization-refinement/refinement-recommendations.md:176:**Problem:** Level recommendation logic is split between `recommend-level.sh` (shell) and `complexity-config.jsonc` (config), creating two sources of truth.\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/074-speckit-template-optimization-refinement/refinement-recommendations.md:182:// scripts/spec/recommend-level.js\n./specs/system-speckit/z_archive/001-fix-command-dispatch/z_archive/074-speckit-template-o