ifact sibling mechanically instead of relying on the agent to read stderr?\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/research.md:135:`recommend-level.sh` scores documentation level and nothing else. Observed at synthesis: a search of its 780 lines for \"related\", \"sibling\", \"series\", \"artifact\" or \"similar\" finds nothing, while a control search for \"level\" finds 73 lines.\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/research.md:401:- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh`, `repair-derived.cjs`, `refresh-track-roots.mjs`, `is-phase-parent.ts`, `recommend-level.sh`\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/research.md:456:**Commands run at synthesis.** All read-only, with output and exit status read: the seeder byte comparison over four templates, posting counts from the committed index, eight trigger lookups (exit 0 or 1 as tabled in section 9), two `generate-trigger-index.mjs --check` runs (exit 1 both times, data directory unchanged), a census walk of `specs/`, modification times of the cited source files and keyword searches with positive controls over the command tree, `create.sh`, the classifier, the graph-metadata schema, the rule scripts, the parity fixture and `recommend-level.sh`.\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/prompts/iteration-9.md:19:Research Topic: How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/prompts/iteration-8.md:19:Research Topic: How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/prompts/iteration-10.md:19:Research Topic: How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/prompts/iteration-7.md:19:Research Topic: How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/prompts/iteration-3.md:19:Research Topic: How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/prompts/iteration-2.md:19:Research Topic: How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/prompts/iteration-6.md:19:Research Topic: How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/prompts/iteration-1.md:19:Research Topic: How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/prompts/iteration-1.md:23:- Q2: Which existing mechanisms already compute relatedness (gate-3-classifier, folder-routing, the trigger index and lookup, the skill advisor, recommend-level.sh, graph-metadata) and which could detect a same-artifact sibling mechanically instead of relying on the agent to read stderr?\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/prompts/iteration-5.md:19:Research Topic: How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/prompts/iteration-4.md:19:Research Topic: How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/iterations/iteration-001.md:10:- **Q2:** Which existing mechanisms already compute relatedness (gate-3-classifier, folder-routing, the trigger index and lookup, the skill advisor, recommend-level.sh, graph-metadata) and which could detect a same-artifact sibling mechanically instead of relying on the agent to read stderr?\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/iterations/iteration-001.md:17:4. Inspected each candidate relatedness mechanism: folder-routing alignment scoring, the trigger index + `lookup-trigger-index.mjs`, `phrase-judge.mjs`, `recommend-level.sh` (negative result), track `graph-metadata.json`, and the skill-advisor identity docs.\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/iterations/iteration-001.md:34:**f-iter001-005 — Five distinct mechanisms exist, but none carries an artifact key.** (a) Folder-routing computes a 0–100 alignment score from conversation keywords against spec-folder name words, save-time only, and already knows how to print \"better matching alternatives\" [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-routing.md:119] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-routing.md:444]. (b) The trigger index plus `lookup-trigger-index.mjs` scores prompt tokens against per-document trigger-phrase postings, with match classes and a `--spec-folder` scope filter, returning the document paths [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs:100] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs:173]; with `--scoring-only` a no-score prompt exits 1 cleanly [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs:22]. (c) Track `graph-metadata.json` mechanically enumerates same-track siblings through `children_ids` and `parent_id` [SOURCE: specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/graph-metadata.json:6], while `depends_on` / `related_to` / `supersedes` are manual and opt-in [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:56]. (d) `phrase-judge.mjs` only gates phrase quality (template-default, editor-fallback, single-token classes) [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lib/phrase-judge.mjs:25]. (e) `recommend-level.sh` contains no relatedness vocabulary (pure level scoring) and skill-advisor routes prompts to skills, not packets — its \"Related skills\" section is resource links [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md:437]. None stores \"the artifact this packet changes\", so mechanical same-artifact detection needs either a new signal or a combination of the trigger-index scoring (resemblance) with artifact extraction from titles/descriptions.\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/iterations/iteration-001.md:57:- **Q2:** Which existing mechanisms already compute relatedness (gate-3-classifier, folder-routing, the trigger index and lookup, the skill advisor, recommend-level.sh, graph-metadata) and which could detect a same-artifact sibling mechanically instead of relying on the agent to read stderr? — Answered at inventory depth: folder-routing alignment scoring, trigger-index phrase scoring, and graph-metadata sibling enumeration are the live signals; classifier, level scorer, and advisor compute none; no mechanism carries an artifact key.\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/iterations/iteration-001.md:87:- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/resource-map.md:2:title: \"Resource Map — How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\"\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/deep-research-strategy.md:42:How to harden the series parent rule, the recent-packets listing in create.sh and the seeded trigger phrases shipped in phase 006 of specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling, and how to improve the UX so agents group related work into phase parents instead of opening many small singleton packets, using the existing related logic (Gate 3 options and gate-3-classifier, phase thresholds, recommend-level.sh, sub-folder versioning, folder routing, trigger index and phrase judge, skill advisor, the speckit plan and complete commands) as the baseline\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/deep-research-strategy.md:49:- [x] Q2: Which existing mechanisms already compute relatedness (gate-3-classifier, folder-routing, the trigger index and lookup, the skill advisor, recommend-level.sh, graph-metadata) and which could detect a same-artifact sibling mechanically instead of relying on the agent to read stderr?\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/deep-research-strategy.md:76:- Q2: Which existing mechanisms already compute relatedness (gate-3-classifier, folder-routing, the trigger index and lookup, the skill advisor, recommend-level.sh, graph-metadata) and which could detect a same-artifact sibling mechanically instead of relying on the agent to read stderr?\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/research/deep-research-strategy.md:166:- Source pointers: the files above plus system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts, runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh, references/structure/folder-routing.md, references/workflows/quick-reference.md sections 8-9, .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs.\n./specs/system-speckit/034-spec-folder-tooling/007-series-parent-review-and-hardening-research/spec.md:73:- Deep research on the series parent rule, the listing and related existing logic: Gate 3 option text, the Gate 3 classifier, phase thresholds, `recommend-level.sh`, the trigger index and the advisor.\n./specs/sk-doc/062-doc-validation-off-switches/tasks.md:37:- [x] T001 Scaffold the packet and score its level (`recommend-level.sh`: Level 2, 50 of 100, no phases)\n./specs/sk-doc/063-security-policy-alignment/goal.md:88:| Level | `recommend-level.sh --loc 150 --files 1` recommended Level 0, and `create.sh` starts at Level 1, so the packet is Level 1 |\n./specs/sk-doc/065-changelog-section-sp